1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,150
Every clan event starts the same way.

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:05,950
Someone says, "we should do a bingo."

3
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:06,750
Everyone agrees.

4
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:11,550
And then one person spends the next two weeks in a spreadsheet,

5
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:14,750
squinting at screenshots of other people's Vorkath kills.

6
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:17,150
Today, that person retires.

7
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:25,750
Open your clan's Manage page, then Events.

8
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:27,350
This is mission control.

9
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:32,550
Live events, drafts, things that already ended, and a button that says Create

10
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:32,950
event.

11
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:34,950
We're going to press it.

12
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:35,350
Bravely.

13
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:37,750
Step one: a name.

14
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,750
Something inspiring, like "Autumn Ladder."

15
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:42,150
Nobody has ever been this creative.

16
00:00:42,150 --> 00:00:43,350
Then a format.

17
00:00:43,350 --> 00:00:46,150
Standard is a plain list of tasks.

18
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:50,150
Bingo is a grid, with bonus points for finishing lines.

19
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:55,350
The fancier formats get their own episodes, because they need the emotional support.

20
00:00:56,150 --> 00:00:58,150
Step two: when it runs.

21
00:00:58,150 --> 00:01:00,150
A start, an end, done.

22
00:01:00,150 --> 00:01:03,750
Or make it repeat, say every weekend this month,

23
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:06,550
and between windows it simply ignores everyone.

24
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:08,150
All times are UTC.

25
00:01:08,150 --> 00:01:08,950
Game time.

26
00:01:08,950 --> 00:01:10,550
No daylight savings surprises.

27
00:01:11,350 --> 00:01:14,150
Step three: how people get on teams.

28
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:19,350
They pick their own, get auto-balanced, drop into a sign-up pool you sort

29
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:22,550
out later, or you assign everyone by hand,

30
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:24,150
like a benevolent dictator.

31
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:26,950
Down here you choose which submissions count.

32
00:01:26,950 --> 00:01:32,150
Everything, plugin only, or anything typed in manually needs an admin's thumbs up.

33
00:01:32,150 --> 00:01:33,750
Trust is a spectrum.

34
00:01:34,550 --> 00:01:35,750
Step four: tasks.

35
00:01:35,750 --> 00:01:40,150
Build them one at a time, grab presets from the library,

36
00:01:40,150 --> 00:01:45,350
or hit Fill for me, and DropTracker drafts a balanced list based on

37
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:50,150
how long the event runs and how much your clan actually plays.

38
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:53,350
The options are casual, regular, and very active.

39
00:01:53,350 --> 00:01:54,150
Be honest.

40
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:56,150
Episode two covers tasks properly.

41
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,150
Step five: teams.

42
00:01:58,150 --> 00:02:03,350
Type a name, add it, paste in a list of players if you

43
00:02:03,350 --> 00:02:04,950
already know who's who.

44
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:08,550
Or skip it and let people sign themselves up.

45
00:02:08,550 --> 00:02:11,750
Your clan, your call, your group chat drama.

46
00:02:12,550 --> 00:02:13,750
Step six: Discord.

47
00:02:13,750 --> 00:02:18,950
Pick where announcements go, where completions go, and where the live leaderboard lives.

48
00:02:18,950 --> 00:02:24,150
It can even create a private channel and a role for every team,

49
00:02:24,150 --> 00:02:26,150
then tidy them up afterwards.

50
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:27,350
Like a butler.

51
00:02:27,350 --> 00:02:28,950
A butler who pings.

52
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:31,750
Last step: the pre-flight check.

53
00:02:31,750 --> 00:02:34,550
If it's all green, launch it now.

54
00:02:34,550 --> 00:02:38,150
Or keep it as a draft and walk away.

55
00:02:38,150 --> 00:02:42,950
Drafts don't expire, don't cost anything, and never ask how you're doing.

56
00:02:43,750 --> 00:02:45,750
Here's what your players see.

57
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:50,550
The board, the standings, their team, and a big sign up button.

58
00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:54,150
And from then on, they just play the game.

59
00:02:54,150 --> 00:02:58,950
The RuneLite plugin sends their drops, kills and personal bests to DropTracker,

60
00:02:58,950 --> 00:03:01,350
and the board fills itself in.

61
00:03:02,150 --> 00:03:03,350
Nobody posts screenshots.

62
00:03:03,350 --> 00:03:04,550
Nobody checks them.

63
00:03:04,550 --> 00:03:06,550
The spreadsheet person is free.

64
00:03:08,350 --> 00:03:09,550
Next time: tasks.

65
00:03:09,550 --> 00:03:14,350
What counts, what doesn't, and why Turael skipping will not save you.
